      "question": "In bioinformatics, how do the concepts of \"similarity\" and \"homology\" differ from one another?",
      "reference_answer": "Similarity refers to the degree of likeness between two sequences expressed as a percentage, whereas homology refers to the common evolutionary ancestry of two sequences based on an assessment of their similarity.",
